---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';

export const prerender = true;
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Editorial, Sourcing, and Corrections Policy · MRX"
  description="How MRX selects sources, separates facts from assumptions, reviews educational content, discloses commercial roles, and corrects material errors."
  path="/editorial-policy/"
  pageType="marketing"
  pageCategory="methodology"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Editorial Policy', path: '/editorial-policy/' },
  ]}
>
  <section class="editorial-hero">
    <div class="container editorial-hero__inner">
      <p class="editorial-eyebrow">Public trust policy</p>
      <h1>Editorial, sourcing, and corrections policy</h1>
      <p>
        MRX publishes educational material for mineral and royalty owners. This policy explains how
        we choose sources, label uncertainty, use AI assistance, review content, disclose commercial
        roles, and correct material errors.
      </p>
      <p class="editorial-updated">Last updated September 1, 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <main class="editorial-body">
    <div class="container editorial-body__grid">
      <div class="editorial-body__content">
        <section aria-labelledby="editorial-purpose">
          <h2 id="editorial-purpose">Purpose and boundaries</h2>
          <p>
            MRX content helps owners organize facts, documents, assumptions, limitations, and next
            questions. It does not replace an independent valuation, fairness opinion, title
            opinion, reserve report, engineering conclusion, or individualized work from an
            attorney, tax professional, accountant, or other qualified professional.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="editorial-sources">
          <h2 id="editorial-sources">Source standards</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Use official agencies, statutes, court or county records, operator filings, and other primary sources when they directly support the claim.</li>
            <li>Use a credible secondary source when it adds explanation or industry context, while identifying the source and its limits.</li>
            <li>State access or review dates when a page, dataset, or process can change.</li>
            <li>Do not treat public production records as proof of private title, ownership, acreage, future drilling, or a single correct price.</li>
            <li>Do not fabricate quotations, transactions, benchmarks, credentials, testimonials, or relationships.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="editorial-evidence">
          <h2 id="editorial-evidence">Facts, assumptions, and examples</h2>
          <p>
            Material factual claims should be traceable to a named source or clearly presented as an
            assumption, scenario, or general educational example. Hypothetical stories must be
            labeled as fictional or illustrative. Privacy-safe examples drawn from real owner
            situations must remove names and details that could identify the person or property.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="editorial-ai">
          <h2 id="editorial-ai">How AI may assist</h2>
          <p>
            AI may help organize research, draft plain-language explanations, identify missing
            questions, or check structure. AI output is not treated as a source. Public content must
            still pass MRX source, editorial, compliance, metadata, and release checks before it is
            published.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="editorial-review">
          <h2 id="editorial-review">Review and attribution</h2>
          <p>
            Articles identify an author or editorial team and may show a review date. Material
            updates should preserve the reviewed topic, revise the update date, and recheck sources,
            links, disclosures, metadata, and visible claims. Questions that require attorney, tax,
            accounting, title, reserve, engineering, or independent valuation work are directed to
            an appropriately qualified professional.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="editorial-commercial">
          <h2 id="editorial-commercial">Commercial-role disclosure</h2>
          <p>
            MRX begins with educational information and a directional underwriter review. There is
            no obligation to sell. MRX may be a buyer in a transaction that results from a review;
            if so, that relationship is disclosed in writing before an agreement is signed. The
            educational review is not presented as an independent valuation or fairness opinion.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="editorial-corrections">
          <h2 id="editorial-corrections">Corrections</h2>
          <p>
            MRX reviews specific correction requests against the cited source and the public page.
            When a material factual error is confirmed, we correct the page, update the review date
            when appropriate, and re-run the applicable release checks. Editorial disagreement,
            unsupported marketing requests, or requests to remove accurate public-source context are
            evaluated separately from factual corrections.
          </p>
          <p>
            Send a page URL, the statement at issue, and the supporting source to
            <!--email_off--><a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('MRX correction request')}`}>{SITE.email}</a><!--/email_off-->.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>

      <aside class="editorial-body__aside">
        <h2>Related trust pages</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/methodology/">Methodology, role, and limitations</a></li>
          <li><a href="/how-it-works/">What the underwriter review covers</a></li>
          <li><a href="/authors/mrx-editorial-team/">MRX Editorial Team</a></li>
          <li><a href="/terms/">Terms and AI disclosure</a></li>
          <li><a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy policy</a></li>
        </ul>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </main>
</MarketingLayout>

<style>
  .editorial-hero {
    padding-block: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6rem);
    background: linear-gradient(145deg, #f7f2e9, #f7f9fa);
  }

  .editorial-hero__inner {
    max-width: 900px;
  }

  .editorial-eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    color: #8b5d16;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .editorial-hero h1,
  .editorial-body h2 {
    color: var(--color-brand-900, #071e34);
  }

  .editorial-hero h1 {
    max-width: 18ch;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 6vw, 4.6rem);
    line-height: 0.98;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
  }

  .editorial-hero p,
  .editorial-body p,
  .editorial-body li {
    color: var(--color-ink-700, #344955);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .editorial-updated {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .editorial-body {
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 5rem);
  }

  .editorial-body__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .editorial-body__content {
    max-width: 78ch;
  }

  .editorial-body__content section + section {
    margin-top: 2.25rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-ink-200, #d7dfe4);
  }

  .editorial-body h2 {
    margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 3vw, 2rem);
  }

  .editorial-body__aside {
    align-self: start;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-ink-200, #d7dfe4);
    border-radius: 1rem;
    background: #f7f9fa;
    padding: 1.4rem;
  }

  .editorial-body__aside h2 {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }

  .editorial-body__aside li + li {
    margin-top: 0.65rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .editorial-body__grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(260px, 0.35fr);
    }
  }
</style>
